<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/040K">Remark <span data-tag="040K">8.5.4.17</span>.</a> In the situation of Notation <a data-tag="040H" href="/tag/040H">8.5.4.15</a>, we can regard $\operatorname{Spine}[\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}]$ as a simplicial subset of the nerve $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}})$, where we regard the set of integers $\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}= \{  \cdots &lt; -2 &lt; -1 &lt; 0 &lt; 1 &lt; 2 &lt; \cdots \} $ as equipped with its usual linear ordering. Moreover, the inclusion $\operatorname{Spine}[\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}] \hookrightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}})$ is inner anodyne (this is a special case of Proposition <a data-tag="00J6" href="/tag/00J6">1.5.7.3</a>). </p>
